(3. Uncompensated Scope Creep via Voice Notes: Buyers often confirm a base stitching rate \(e.g., Rs. 58/piece\) and later send) Tj
T* (informal voice notes requesting extra complex operations \(e.g., collar embroidery, double-needle stitching, bio-wash\) without) Tj
T* (revising the price. Under Section 62 of the *Indian Contract Act, 1872*, unilateral alterations to contract scope without reciprocal) Tj
T* (consideration are void.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.216 g
42.5196850393700814 726.2364566929134071 Td
(4. Floating or Uncertain Rates \(Section 29 Contract Act\): Agreements settled on vague terms like *"market rate dekh lenge"* or) Tj
T* (*"Rs 90 to 105 decide karenge"* are legally void for uncertainty under Section 29 of the Indian Contract Act, leaving job-workers) Tj
T* (with no legal basis to recover dues.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
